From ad772e74f75d305fa729836bd9a980552458d9ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:22:57 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/9] sparc64: advance the PROM console buffer by bytes
 written

The firmware write service returns the number of bytes accepted. Advance
the buffer by that count after a short write, rather than by the remaining
length, so subsequent calls send the next bytes of the original buffer.

Fixes: 595a251c0740 ("sparc: Write to prom console using indirect buffer.")
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
index 86dace787ae6..d58b42f0658f 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
@@ -41,6 +41,6 @@ void prom_console_write_buf(const char *buf, int len)
 		if (n < 0)
 			continue;
 		len -= n;
-		buf += len;
+		buf += n;
 	}
 }
